# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots apache2 serving the vulnerable read.php (no
# open_basedir) and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * httpd is ALREADY serving the LFI endpoint when the agent starts, which
#     makes the "set open_basedir but never restarted apache" case detectable
#     (apache reads php.ini only at startup);
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting apache cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART apache after editing the
# apache2 php.ini; an un-restarted server keeps honouring file_get_contents on
# arbitrary paths and verify.sh FAILS.
